# specs/ledger: the admission record.
#
# One line per admitted spec:   service | spec_version | sha256 | admitted | source
#
# scripts/spec-intake-check.sh recomputes every digest on every run, so a spec edited
# after admission is a red build. That is what makes "admitted verbatim" a checkable
# property rather than a promise (specs/README.md, "Admission: verbatim, or flagged").
#
# The record is keyed on the PATH, specs/admitted/<service>/<spec_version>.md, because the
# path is the slot a consumer resolves. Records are never removed: a superseded spec stays
# admitted, and what a spec said when a decision was taken is evidence.
